Check environment configuration

Verifies that your environment is properly configured for Antithesis testing.
Runs health checks — container runtime, docker compose, the tenant and container
registry settings, and your credentials (stored by `snouty login`, or set in the
ANTITHESIS_* environment variables). A missing registry is a warning, because
only `snouty launch` needs it. To see the settings that snouty resolved, run
`snouty settings show`.

The credential can be a sign-in or an API key from `snouty login`, an API key in
ANTITHESIS_API_KEY, or a GitHub Actions OIDC token.

doctor also contacts the Antithesis API. It confirms that your credential works,
reports the API and tenant versions, and warns when the tenant release is too
old for a command. It also tells you when your tenant has an Antithesis registry
that the registry setting does not use. Use --offline to skip the checks that
contact the API.

The command fails if any required check fails.

With --json, the output is one JSON object, with the fields ok and checks. ok is
false when any check has status error. checks is a list of checks, each with the
fields id, status (ok, warn or error) and message.

Examples:
  snouty doctor
  snouty doctor --offline

Usage: snouty doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --offline
          Skip the checks that contact the Antithesis API

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Print one JSON object

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
